</head>

<body>

    <div class="puzzle">
        <div class="center">
            <h2>Time to log in to the Network</h2> <br />
            <img src="https://games.bitsmasher.net/web/static/images/archie1.jpg" alt="Made with vi on an IBM 8088"><br />
            <em>“Indeed, the safest road to Hell is the gradual one—the gentle slope, soft underfoot, without sudden turnings, without milestones, without signposts.” – C. S. Lewis</em> <br />
        </div>
   </div>

    <p>

    <h3>Log in with your SSH key</h3>

    <ul>
        <li>Your home directory is already mounted with all your files.</li>
        <li>The public half of your SSH key is already in /home/sly/.ssh/authorized_keys</li>
        <li>Your first challenge is to log in via SSH to your shell account.</li>
        <li>The hostname is &quot;node2&quot; and the IPv4 address is &quot;10.10.12.2&quot;</li>
    </ul>

    It may make sense for you to copy the private half or your SSH keys into ~/.ssh on the network. If you
    are worried about security, you can make a new key pair solely for lab use. 

    <div class="puzzle">
        <div class="center">
            <form action="/submission" method="get">
                <table border="1">
                    
                    <tr>
                        <th>Date</th>
                        <th>Puzzle</th>
                        <th>Flag</th>
                    </tr>

                    <tr>
                        <td>May 23, 2025</td>
                        <td>Puzzle2 <input type="hidden" name="puzzle" value="puzzle2-1"></td>                
                        <td>Flag: <input type="text" name="flag" placeholder="probably-wrong"></td>
                    </tr>

                </table>

                <input type="submit" value="Submit">

            </form>
        </div>
    </div>


    <h3>Obtain a Kerboeros ticket</h3>

    Once you are logged in to your shell, you are ready to obtain your Kerberos credentials. This will help you
    navigate around the network without having to type your password over and over.

    <div class="puzzle">
        <div class="center">
